{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "Structural patterns (design.md §5). The pattern analyzer NEVER forces a verdict — it",
    "contributes weight and category hints only, and its total is capped at 0.5 so that a",
    "verbose scam cannot stack a dozen weak patterns and drown out the classifier.",
    "",
    "Patterns run against NormalizedMessage.normalized: NFKC, zero-width stripped, whitespace",
    "collapsed, Locale.ROOT lowercased. Latin patterns are therefore written lowercase and",
    "need no case flag. Devanagari, Bengali, Tamil and Telugu are caseless.",
    "",
    "`suppress_if` is the hard-negative guard. The single most common genuine bank SMS in",
    "India is an OTP delivery containing the words 'do not share this OTP with anyone'. A",
    "naive share.*otp pattern fires on it, and design.md §12 requires all 15 genuine bank",
    "fixtures to return SAFE with zero tolerance. Any rule whose vocabulary overlaps a genuine",
    "message needs one of these.",
    "",
    "Weights are per-rule contributions before the 0.5 cap. They are ordered by how much a hit",
    "narrows the space of innocent explanations, not by how alarming the wording is: urgency is",
    "cheap and common in genuine marketing, whereas a request to hand over an OTP has almost no",
    "innocent reading at all."
  ],

  "patterns": [
    {
      "id": "otp_solicit_en",
      "lang": ["EN", "HI_LATN"],
      "pattern": "\\b(share|send|tell|provide|forward|give|submit|reply with|revert with)\\s+(?:me\\s+|us\\s+|the\\s+|your\\s+|ur\\s+|this\\s+|that\\s+|it\\s+|a\\s+)*\\b(otp|one\\s?time\\s?password|o\\.t\\.p|pin|cvv|verification code|security code|atm pin)\\b",
      "suppress_if": "\\b(?:never|do not|don'?t|dont|no one|nobody|not)\\s+(?:\\w+\\s+){0,3}?(?:share|shares|sharing|disclose|reveal|give|tell|ask|asks|request|requests)\\b",
      "evidence": "OTP_SOLICITATION",
      "severity": "CRITICAL",
      "weight": 0.35,
      "category_hints": { "KYC_PHISHING": 0.4, "UPI_COLLECT": 0.3 }
    },
